{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260909-8d05512ce3c9a9ece43562be","sequence":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:19:05.738097Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"a70c800e-de9d-4644-9772-0a026a44f0b6"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"BUG-260830-j1o8av","element_type":"bug"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260909-b9d51eefc82d3b5e8bd769c4","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"description","before":{"kind":"text","text":"Default ./setup.sh fails on current Homebrew after LLVM 23 no longer provides /opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin/lldb-mcp. Detect the supported LLDB package/helper location or produce a typed actionable refusal without breaking unrelated global setup. Preserve AGENTS_INFRA_SKIP_LLDB_MCP=1 as the explicit bypass."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Default ./setup.sh dies before building or installing any binary on current Homebrew:\n\n  Homebrew llvm did not provide expected helper: /opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin/lldb-mcp\n\nAn optional debugging integration therefore blocks the entire installation, including the agents-infra and model-harness binaries that have nothing to do with LLDB.\n\nInvestigation on 2026-09-09 settles the question the original report left open, namely whether a supported helper location exists to detect:\n\n- Homebrew llvm 23.1.1 ships no lldb and no lldb-mcp at all; /opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin contains neither.\n- The Apple LLDB from Xcode (lldb-2100.0.17.203) has no MCP support; its help lists no mcp command.\n- The wrapper this bootstrap previously published, /opt/homebrew/bin/lldb-mcp, execs the now-absent /opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin/lldb-mcp, so it is broken rather than usable. install_lldb_mcp does not notice, because it treats an existing lldb-mcp as satisfied only when its path differs from the wrapper it publishes, and here they are the same path.\n\nThere is no supported source to install lldb-mcp from. Owner decision on 2026-09-09: remove the integration rather than keep repairing detection for a helper no distribution ships.\n\nThe generic MCP mechanism is untouched: a project that obtains an lldb-mcp binary by other means can still declare it in its own registry. What goes away is the bootstrap that installs it and the shared server definition that promises it."}},{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"relux-agents-infra setup/bootstrap source, Homebrew package detection, generated wrapper verification, docs and fake/static tests. Do not require a live LLDB target."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"scripts/setup.sh bootstrap and its skip flag; the shared servers.lldb definition in .configs/codex-mcp-servers.toml; lldb references in README.md, SKILL.md, and .instructions/INSTRUCTIONS_TOOLS.md. Generic MCP wiring and unrelated test fixtures that merely use lldb as a sample server name stay as they are."}},{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"On current Homebrew macOS the default setup either installs and verifies a real supported lldb-mcp helper from the correct package or fails before partial wrapper publication with a precise remediation; LLVM 22 compatibility and the skip flag remain covered; no unrelated global runtime files drift."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"setup.sh builds and installs both binaries on a machine with no lldb-mcp anywhere, with no LLDB step and no skip flag needed; no shared registry entry promises an lldb server; docs no longer claim setup installs an lldb-mcp wrapper; go vet and go test pass."}}]}
